<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Somali Democratic Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1969 CE – 1991 CE · capital Mogadishu</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Somalia under the military rule of Siad Barre, a socialist state whose defeat in the Ogaden and repression of clans led to its collapse in 1991.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On 21 October 1969, days after the assassination of President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdirashid-ali-shermarke">Abdirashid Ali Shermarke</a>, the army led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siad-barre">Mohamed Siad Barre</a> seized power in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/somali-republic">Somali Republic</a>. A Supreme Revolutionary Council suspended the constitution, banned parties and renamed the country the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somali</a> Democratic Republic, declaring scientific socialism in 1970.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siad-barre">Barre</a> allied with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, nationalised the economy and in 1972 made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somali</a> a written official language in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> script, followed by mass literacy campaigns. In 1977 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/somalia">Somalia</a> invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ogaden">Ogaden</a>, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviets</a> switched sides and Somali forces were defeated in 1978. Barre then relied increasingly on his own clan alliances, and his forces bombed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hargeisa">Hargeisa</a> in 1988, killing thousands of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/isaaq-sultanate">Isaaq</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Rebel movements, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somali-national-movement">Somali National Movement</a> in the north and the United <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somali</a> Congress in the south, closed in, and in January 1991 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siad-barre">Barre</a> fled <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-mogadishu">Mogadishu</a>. The state collapsed into civil war; the north declared itself the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-somaliland">Republic of Somaliland</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/somali-democratic-republic.jpg" alt="Somali Democratic Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: see upload history · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Somalia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1969 CE – 1991 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mogadishu</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Siad Barre</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Somali, Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/somalia">Somalia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Siad Barre's Somalia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1980&amp;focus=somali-democratic-republic" aria-label="Somali Democratic Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5939 2101 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Somali Democratic Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6259 2357L6259 2357M6259 2357L6259 2357M6259 2357L6216 2076"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6259 2357h0M6259 2357h0M6216 2076h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6259 2357h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6259 2357h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Mogadishu. <a href="/atlas?year=1980&amp;focus=somali-democratic-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
